   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">In Non\u2011Restoring Division, if remainder R is negative, the next step does:</strong></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 308,
   "TYPE": "mcq",
   "key": 25203
  },
  {
   "_id": 25401,
   "ANSWER": 2,
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OPT_1": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Based on the size of the divisor</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_2": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Based on the sign of the remainder after the operation&nbsp;</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_3": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Bsed on whether the dividend is even or odd</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_4": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Randomly assigned during each cycle</strong></p>\n",
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">In non-restoring division, how is the quotient bit decided at each step?</strong></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 308,
   "TYPE": "mcq",
   "key": 25401
  },
  {
   "_id": 25402,
   "ANSWER": 2,
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OPT_1": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">It uses fewer registers</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_2": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">It does not require restoring after every subtraction&nbsp;</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_3": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">It produces more accurate results</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_4": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">It can divide both positive and negative numbers directly</strong></p>\n",
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">What is the primary advantage of the non-restoring division algorithm over the restoring division algorithm?</strong></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 308,
   "TYPE": "mcq",
   "key": 25402
  },
  {
   "_id": 25403,
   "ANSWER": 2,
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OPT_1": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Discard the remainder</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_2": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Add the divisor to the remainder&nbsp;</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_3": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Subtract the divisor from the remainder</strong></p>\n",
   "OPT_4": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Multiply the quotient by 2</strong></p>\n",
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">What is the final step in the non-restoring division algorithm if the remainder is negative after all iterations?</strong></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 308,
   "TYPE": "mcq",
   "key": 25403
  },
  {
   "_id": 25406,
   "ANSWER": 3,
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OPT_1": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">The number of shifts is always 2n</strong><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "OPT_2": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">The number of shifts is n+1</strong><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "OPT_3": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">The number of shifts is exactly n&nbsp;</strong><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "OPT_4": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">It depends on the size of the divisor only</strong></p>\n",
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p><strong data-end=\"78\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"0\">Which of the following is true regarding the number of shifts in a non-restoring division algorithm for n-bit operands?</strong><br />\n&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 308,
   "TYPE": "mcq",
   "key": 25406
  }
